  "result": "Based on my investigation of the codebase and documentation, I found a discrepancy in the permission gates.\n\nThe documentation in `screen-settings-billing-flags-webhooks.md` at line 86 states that the feature flag settings page requires:\n\n**\"Permission required: `org:manage_flags` (member and above) — 404 otherwise\"**\n\nHowever, according to the code:\n1. The ROLE_MATRIX in `src/lib/permissions.ts` line 30 defines: `\"org:manage_flags\": \"admin\"`\n2. The feature flag settings page at `src/app/(dashboard)/[orgSlug]/settings/flags/page.tsx` lines 41-47 checks `can(actor, \"org:manage_flags\", ...)` and denies access (404) unless the actor has admin role\n3. Multiple requirements documents (`membership-and-roles.md`, `feature-flags.md`, `action-members-billing-and-flags.md`) consistently state that `org:manage_flags` requires `admin` minimum\n\nThe documentation falsely claims **members and above** can manage feature flags, but the code enforces **admin minimum only**. This is the only discrepancy between documentation and code enforcement in the role-based permission gates.\n\nANSWER: docs/ui/screen-settings-billing-flags-webhooks.md",
